# Git is NOT the store for backfilled history — 30 days of Morpho on ONE chain
# is already 50 MB, and a full two-year run across every chain is multiple GB.
# That output belongs in object storage, replayed into yield-tracer through
# POST /ingest/lending-history (LENDING_HISTORY_BACKFILL_PLAN.md §0.8).
#
# The two exceptions are the sources that serve a ROLLING window — Compound V3
# (30 days) and LlamaLend (100 snapshots). Those are a ratchet, not a backfill:
# uncaptured days are gone for good, they are small (~2.5 MB/month combined),
# and committing them is what makes the daily GH Action a durable record until
# the bucket exists. Enforced here rather than left to convention, because the
# failure mode is a multi-GB accidental commit.
*
!.gitignore
!manifest.json
!COMPOUND_V3/
!COMPOUND_V3/**
!LLAMALEND/
!LLAMALEND/**
# Vault-side rolling windows (added 2026-08-25 with @lending-owners/fetcher-vaults):
# Cap caps at 1 year (deeper combos are WAF-403'd), Gearbox at 1 year (no `all`
# period). Small (~1 MB/year combined) and captured by the same daily Action —
# without these exceptions the CI runner's capture is discarded with the runner.
!VAULT_CAP/
!VAULT_CAP/**
!VAULT_GEARBOX/
!VAULT_GEARBOX/**

# Savings-side rolling windows (added 2026-09-09 with the savings modules):
# Sky and Spark are capped by Blockanalitica's 365-day `days_ago` whitelist,
# Falcon at 365 points, Tori at 30, YO's yield route at 30 days. Together they
# are ~250 KB/year — the same ratchet argument as Cap and Gearbox, at a tenth
# of the size.
#
# AAVE_V3 is deliberately NOT here despite being in `DECAYING`: its 365-day
# window is ~11 MB per run and grows with every chain, and its accumulator is
# reconstructible from archival RPC, so it is a bucket problem, not a git one.
!VAULT_SKY/
!VAULT_SKY/**
!VAULT_SPARK/
!VAULT_SPARK/**
!VAULT_FALCON/
!VAULT_FALCON/**
!VAULT_TORI/
!VAULT_TORI/**
!VAULT_YO/
!VAULT_YO/**
